1. Vendored agent skills
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source of truth:   .github/skills-external/
Generated mirrors: .agents/skills/, .claude/skills/, .codex/skills/,
                   .opencode/skills/

These directories contain skills authored by third parties and vendored into
this repository by the sync engine (src/ml_python_base/skills_sync). The
mirrors are generated copies of the same upstream content, so a redistribution
of this repository redistributes each component five times. `skills-lock.json`
records content hashes and sync timestamps; it does not record provenance.

1.1 Superpowers skill collection
    Upstream project: Superpowers (https://github.com/obra/superpowers)
    Author:           Jesse Vincent (obra)

    Components:
      brainstorming
      executing-plans
      finishing-a-development-branch
      requesting-code-review
      subagent-driven-development
      test-driven-development
      using-git-worktrees
      writing-clearly-and-concisely
      writing-plans

    Seven of these reference the upstream `superpowers:` skill namespace and
    `~/.config/superpowers/` directly in their SKILL.md; `test-driven-
    development` and `writing-clearly-and-concisely` are attributed to the same
    collection by their sync origin rather than by in-file evidence.

    UPSTREAM LICENSE: NOT YET CONFIRMED. No LICENSE file accompanied these
    components when they were vendored, and none of them carries author or
    license frontmatter. The upstream terms MUST be confirmed and recorded here
    -- including the upstream copyright notice, if its license requires
    retaining one -- before this repository is distributed outside the
    organization.

1.2 ui-ux-pro-max
    Upstream project: not recorded at sync time.
    Author:           not recorded at sync time.

    UPSTREAM LICENSE: NOT YET CONFIRMED, and the provenance itself is unknown --
    nothing in this repository records where this component was imported from.
    Establish its origin and terms, or remove it, before external distribution.

